codex
The exact summary is present, but its guard is blocked by the semantics leaving `clampHi(K, len, 1)` symbolic at the equality boundary `K == len`. I’m adding the mathematically derived simplification `clampHi(I,L,STEP)=I` for `I≤L` and nonnegative step, plus explicit bridge priority so the proven exact summary is considered before one-step loop unfolding.
